# Multi-Tenant Data Access Rules

## Always scope queries by tenant_id

Every DB query must include the `tenant_id` filter. Never write a query that can return rows from multiple tenants.

```java
// BAD — returns rows from all tenants
List<Employee> all = employeeRepository.findAll();

// GOOD — always scoped
List<Employee> scoped = employeeRepository.findByTenantId(tenantId);
```

## Tenant context resolution

Read tenant context from the request header `X-Tenant-ID` (set by Kong after JWT validation). Never resolve tenant from user input.

```java
String tenantId = request.getHeader("X-Tenant-ID"); // set by Kong gateway
// Then set on DB connection:
entityManager.createNativeQuery("SET app.current_tenant_id = :t").setParameter("t", tenantId).executeUpdate();
```

## Schema routing (Pro tier)

For Pro tenants, switch `search_path` before any query. Use a request-scoped interceptor — do not rely on callers to remember.

## Never cross service DB boundaries

- Ingestion Service reads/writes `ingestion-db` only.
- Employee Profile Service reads/writes `profile-db` only.
- If you need data from another service, consume its Kafka events or call its REST API.

## Redis keyspace prefix

All Redis keys must be prefixed: `{entity}:{tenant_id}:{...}`. Example: `profile:tenant_acme_corp:emp_123`.
